points.description:
You look at the food you want. A laptop webcam tracks your eyes and selects it. A robot arm then brings the food to you. One small camera on the arm's wrist finds the food on the table, and the arm slows down as your face gets closer.
What runs on real hardware today:

eye-tracking selection;
the arm's feeding motion;
food recognition from the wrist camera;
the arm moving under the control code fr
